full_text:
Ford is building cars that "talk" with traffic lights, road signs and pedestrians. At CES 2019 in Las Vegas on 8 January, the company showed a demonstration of its smart traffic technology, which includes the use of cameras and radar sensors to communicate with the infrastructure of the city. According to the company, this system is designed to reduce congestion, accidents and improve traffic flow.
In particular, the new Ford technology includes features such as:
Communicating traffic lights that can detect when a driver approaches and adjust the green light time accordingly;
Radar sensors that detect pedestrians and cyclists and alert the driver, as well as slow down the vehicle accordingly;
Real-time updates on traffic and road conditions, displayed on a dashboard screen or sent to a mobile device;
Predictive maintenance

